---

<DocsLayout
  title="aegis scan"
  description="Review a repository, map its attack surface, run generated security tests, and report verified findings."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "CLI reference", href: "/docs/cli/" }, { label: "scan" }]}
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="name">NAME</h2>
  <p><code>aegis scan</code> — review, test, and report in a single pass.</p>

  <h2 id="synopsis">SYNOPSIS</h2>
  <CodeBlock title="synopsis">aegis scan [PATH ...]
    [--diff=REVISION_RANGE] [--rules=PACK,...] [--format=FORMAT]
    [--output=PATH] [--min-severity=SEVERITY] [--fail-on=SEVERITY]
    [--include-unverified] [--no-tests] [--timeout=DURATION]
    [--concurrency=N] [GLOBAL_FLAGS ...]</CodeBlock>

  <h2 id="description">DESCRIPTION</h2>
  <p>
    <code>aegis scan</code> runs the full pipeline. It reviews the selected
    files, resolves entry points and data flows into an attack surface,
    generates targeted tests for each candidate finding, executes them, and
    prints the findings it could verify.
  </p>
  <p>
    Progress is written to stderr and results to stdout, so the command can be
    piped without extra flags. With <code>--output</code>, results are written
    to a file instead.
  </p>
  <p>
    Analysis state is stored under <code>.aegis/</code> and reused by
    <a href="/docs/cli/test/"><code>aegis test</code></a> and
    <a href="/docs/cli/report/"><code>aegis report</code></a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="examples">EXAMPLES</h2>
  <p>Scan the current repository:</p>
  <CodeBlock title="shell">aegis scan</CodeBlock>

  <p>Scan only what a pull request changes:</p>
  <CodeBlock title="shell">aegis scan --diff origin/main...HEAD</CodeBlock>

  <p>Scan two directories with a specific set of rule packs:</p>
  <CodeBlock title="shell">aegis scan src services --rules core,web-api</CodeBlock>

  <p>Produce SARIF for a code-scanning dashboard and fail only on critical findings:</p>
  <CodeBlock title="shell">aegis scan --format sarif --output aegis.sarif --fail-on critical</CodeBlock>

  <p>Review without executing tests, for an environment where the service cannot run:</p>
  <CodeBlock title="shell">aegis scan --no-tests --include-unverified</CodeBlock>

  <h2 id="positional">POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>[PATH ...]</dt>
    <dd>
      Files or directories to scan, relative to the repository root. Defaults to
      the paths in <code>scan.include</code>, or the whole tree. Paths given
      here are still filtered by <code>scan.exclude</code>.
    </dd>
  </dl>

  <h2 id="flags">FLAGS</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>--diff=REVISION_RANGE</dt>
    <dd>
      Restrict the review to files changed in a Git revision range, for example
      <code>origin/main...HEAD</code>. Requires full history in the checkout.
    </dd>
    <dt>--rules=PACK,...</dt>
    <dd>
      Comma-separated rule packs, or a path to a directory of rule files.
      Overrides <code>rules.packs</code>. See <a href="/docs/rulesets/">Rulesets</a>.
    </dd>
    <dt>--format=text|json|sarif|markdown</dt>
    <dd>Output format. Default is <code>text</code>.</dd>
    <dt>--output=PATH</dt>
    <dd>Write results to <code>PATH</code> instead of stdout.</dd>
    <dt>--min-severity=critical|high|medium|low</dt>
    <dd>Omit findings below this severity from the output. Default is <code>low</code>.</dd>
    <dt>--fail-on=critical|high|medium|low|never</dt>
    <dd>
      Severity at which the command exits with status <code>1</code>. Default is
      <code>high</code>. <code>never</code> always exits <code>0</code> when the
      scan itself succeeds.
    </dd>
    <dt>--include-unverified</dt>
    <dd>
      Also report candidate findings that tests could not reproduce. They are
      marked <code>unverified</code> and never trigger <code>--fail-on</code>.
    </dd>
    <dt>--no-tests</dt>
    <dd>Skip test generation and execution. Equivalent to <code>tests.enabled: false</code>.</dd>
    <dt>--timeout=DURATION</dt>
    <dd>Per-test timeout, such as <code>90s</code> or <code>3m</code>. Default is <code>90s</code>.</dd>
    <dt>--concurrency=N</dt>
    <dd>Number of parallel analysis workers. Default is the number of CPUs.</dd>
    <dt>--baseline=PATH</dt>
    <dd>
      Suppress findings already present in a previous result file, so only new
      findings are reported.
    </dd>
  </dl>
  <Callout type="note">
    <p>
      <code>--fail-on</code> considers verified findings only. A candidate shown
      with <code>--include-unverified</code> never changes the exit status.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="output">OUTPUT</h2>
  <p>
    <code>text</code> is designed for terminals and is not a stable interface.
    Parse <code>json</code> or <code>sarif</code> in automation; both follow a
    versioned schema and changes are announced in the release notes.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock title="json">{`{
  "version": "1.8.2",
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "sql-injection",
      "severity": "critical",
      "verified": true,
      "location": { "path": "src/api/users.ts", "line": 84 },
      "evidence": { "test": "sqli-users-id", "result": "unexpected_rows" },
      "remediation": "Use parameterized queries or an ORM."
    }
  ],
  "summary": { "critical": 1, "high": 0, "medium": 0, "low": 0 }
}`}</CodeBlock>

  <h2 id="exit-status">EXIT STATUS</h2>
  <p>
    <code>0</code> when no finding met <code>--fail-on</code>, <code>1</code>
    when one did, and other codes on error. See
    <a href="/docs/exit-codes/">Exit codes</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="see-also">SEE ALSO</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/docs/cli/init/">aegis init</a>,
    <a href="/docs/cli/test/">aegis test</a>,
    <a href="/docs/cli/report/">aegis report</a>,
    <a href="/docs/configuration/">Configuration</a>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
